<header><p class="enc-kicker">Event</p><h1 class="enc-title">Convertibility Plan</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1991">1991</a>–<a href="/years/2002">2002</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/20th-century">20th century</a> · Also known as Convertibility Law</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Convertibility Plan was the Argentine monetary system introduced in 1991 by President <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/carlos-menem">Carlos Menem</a>'s economy minister Domingo Cavallo, which fixed the peso at par with the US dollar and backed the money supply with reserves. It ended hyperinflation and drew foreign investment, but left the economy uncompetitive and indebted, and it collapsed in the crisis of 2001–2002.</p></div>
